    "heightBasis": "Retained exact-QID way/77102132/Q991832 matches current main35184449190964 (24 vertices rather than earlier34). Current dome component35185413897395 retains20 raw vertices and height100m. Both controls retain all44 vertices/tags by rigid rotation with no rescale. Native+X eastern eight-column portico, -X western rear and lateral towers sign retained heading0.494588533929rad. Existing Wikidata facts height100m, length120m and width40m remain verbatim; their measurement datum/scope is unspecified. Current mapped whole is about116.4m long/94.4m across including lateral tower wings, while central body is about43.8m wide. No artificial scaling forces the40m fact onto the whole envelope. The100m fact and dome tag are retained without forcing that measurement onto the entrance-floor datum. Picture proportions guide an estimated90m exterior tip above the model floor; crypt/basement-to-cross datum remains unresolved. Other heights and all internal partitions are picture estimates: main wall34m/shallow copper roof40m; portico columns1..30.5m, entablature34m/pediment43m; side links34m with open ground arches; tower base34m, octagonal belfry35..49m, green cap55m/tip58m; drum42..63m/cornice66m, green dome84m/orb86m/cross90m. Drum radius/center follows mapped component, with estimated24 exterior columns and recessed rectangular bays. Lower side paired arched fields, high lunettes, rear parapet/roof surfaces, pilasters and decoration are simplified. No survey/engineering accuracy claimed.",
    "scope": "Individual Esztergom Basilica: eight-column classical open portico/triangular pediment/inset timber portal, broad pale rectangular masonry body with paired round windows/high lunettes and rear parapet terrace. Two lateral tower wings with genuine round arch passages and balustrades, octagonal dark-louvered upper stages/green domes/crosses. Dominant tall pale colonnaded central drum, recessed rectangular window bays, heavy circular cornice and green ribbed copper dome/orb/cross. Four existing shared stone/continuous limestone/copper/wood graphs, metric UVs, linear tints and four browser levels. Fine Corinthian sculpture/reliefs/inscriptions, interiors and exact hilltop threshold joins remain approximate or excluded."
